# Agent Topology — Ultimate Memory Stack General Edition

> **Purpose:** Define the 4-peer agent topology that the harness should support. On Claude Code, these agents execute via Claude's Task tool. On OpenClaw, this spec is **advisory** until OpenClaw runtime supports peer-agent spawning.
> **Loaded:** Tier 1 / WARM — auto-loaded every session.
> **Budget:** ~6K chars.

---

## Flat hierarchy

```
                    USER (approves all)
                          │
                    ORCHESTRATOR
              (main harness instance)
          ┌────────┬────────┬────────┐
          │        │        │        │
       WARDEN   SENTINEL   VAULT   CLERK
      (security) (vetting) (memory)  (PM)
```

All 4 agents are **peers** reporting to the Orchestrator. No agent is subordinate to another. The Orchestrator brokers all inter-agent communication.

---

## Agents

| Agent | Codename | When to spawn | Tool restrictions |
|---|---|---|---|
| Chief Security Agent | **Warden** | Security oversight, session audits, posture reports, CVE impact assessment | Read, Glob, Grep, WebSearch, WebFetch |
| Security Vetting Agent | **Sentinel** | Before installing ANY skill / tool / MCP / hook / plugin | Read, Glob, Grep, WebFetch, WebSearch |
| Memory Stack Agent | **Vault** | Session start/end, storing/retrieving persistent context | Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep |
| Project Management Agent | **Clerk** | Task tracking, kanban, daily logs, status reports | Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep, Bash |

---

## Spawning protocol

### Before installing any new tool/skill

1. Spawn Warden for pre-vetting context (CVE history, author reputation, conflict analysis)
2. Spawn Sentinel with the tool's source URL/files + Warden's context
3. Wait for Sentinel's Security Vetting Report
4. Warden reviews Sentinel's report and adds final assessment
5. Present combined report to the user
6. Only proceed if the user approves
7. Log the vetting via Vault to `memory/security/`

### At session start

1. Read `BOOTSTRAP.md` for entry-point
2. Spawn Warden for config integrity check
3. Spawn Vault to retrieve relevant context for pending tasks
4. Spawn Clerk to load the kanban + generate standup
5. Remind the user to review any pending logs

### At session end

1. Spawn Warden for session security audit
2. Spawn Clerk to update Daily_Activity_Log
3. Spawn Vault to store session context + archive Warden's audit
4. Update `BOOTSTRAP.md` with next-session entry-point

---

## Parallel spawning rules

| Pair | Can run parallel? | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Warden + Clerk | YES | Independent domains (security vs PM) |
| Warden + Sentinel | YES (pre-vetting only) | Warden researches context while Sentinel analyzes code |
| Sentinel + Clerk | YES | Independent |
| Vault + Clerk | NO | Both write to logs |
| Vault + Warden | NO | Vault archives Warden's output; Warden must complete first |

